  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "波動力學、熱力學和光學",
    "sub_ename": "WAVE, HEAT&LIGHT",
    "describe_ch": "這是一門以理工領域學生為對象並結合微積分的普通物理課程. 課程內容以光學和熱力學的理論和應用為主。探討的主題包含 波動、幾何光學、波動光學(例如 光干涉、光繞射、光偏極)、熱、材料熱學性質和熱力學定律。延伸主題還將包含狹義相對論與近代物理。每週另有實驗課三小時，包括各實驗單元的原理介紹與操作，透過實際的實驗與操作實習協助學生進一步理解。",
    "describe_eh": "This is a calculus-based general physics for students majoring in engineering or sciences. The major contents are the general principles and applications of optics and thermodynamics. Topics include wave, geometric optics, wave optics (including interference, diffraction, and polarization), heat, thermal properties of matter, and thermodynamics’ laws. The topics will also be extended to special relativity and modern physics. Besides lectures, we’ll also focus on the problem solving skills as well as the basic mathematical modeling.",
